### Concrete Correction:
```typescript
if (items.length > 0) {
    const first = items[0].name;
}
```

### Regression Example:
Before:
```typescript
const first = items[0].name; // items may be empty
```

After:
```typescript
if (items.length > 0) {
    const first = items[0].name;
}
```

In the original code, the variable `first` was being assigned a value from an empty array, which would result in an error. The corrected version checks if the array is not empty before attempting to access its first element.
